  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration (config_041: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc=0.725) has only been tested with one RNA encoder (scvi_n200). The RNA encoder is a major unexplored design axis, and RNA is the dominant modality (RNA-only multi-profile already reaches 0.650 vs image-only at ~0.23). Question: config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable swap of RNA encoder (scvi_n200 → scgpt) within the best-performing regime, directly isolating the effect of RNA representation quality. Why best next experiment: Under a limited budget, resolving whether a different RNA foundation model (scgpt) meaningfully shifts performance in the top-performing configuration is the highest-information experiment. If scgpt improves, it opens a new optimization axis; if it matches or underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is sufficient and redirects effort to other variables (e.g., image encoder or fusion). This avoids changing multiple factors simultaneously and builds directly on the strongest evidence we have."
